{
  "name": "35 · Payslip Sender (Kaamchor AI · MAP 3.0)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 35 · Payslip Sender\nOn the 1st of every month it reads last month's **Payroll** sheet, checks every row adds up (code + AI sanity check), then turns each payslip into a **PDF** and emails it to the employee. If anything looks wrong, **nothing is sent** and the owner gets a WhatsApp with the problems.\n\n**Setup (15 min)**\n1. Google Sheets nodes: add a **Google Sheets OAuth2** credential and paste your sheet link in place of YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_URL. Tab **Payroll**: Key, Month (yyyy-mm), Name, Email, Basic, HRA, Allowances, Overtime, Deductions, PF, ESI, TDS, Net pay, Days worked, Sent.\n2. PDF: run the free Gotenberg converter once (`docker run -d -p 3000:3000 gotenberg/gotenberg:8`) and replace YOUR_GOTENBERG_URL (e.g. http://localhost:3000).\n3. Gmail nodes: add a **Gmail OAuth2** credential.\n4. WhatsApp nodes: add a **WhatsApp Business Cloud API** credential and replace YOUR_PHONE_NUMBER_ID with your Phone Number ID (Meta → WhatsApp → API setup). Replace YOUR_OWNER_WHATSAPP with the owner's WhatsApp number in 91XXXXXXXXXX format.\n5. AI model node: add an **Anthropic** credential (or swap the model node for OpenAI / Gemini).\n\nThe AI never changes numbers; it only checks them.",
        "height": 679,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "1b3e04cf-7de2-40f3-af03-e36d559cbcb7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -500,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "months",
              "triggerAtDayOfMonth": 1,
              "triggerAtHour": 10
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "34f0bf3c-a92a-444c-84d1-06d1bc70fd90",
      "name": "1st of month 10 AM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "url",
          "value": "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_URL"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Payroll"
        },
        "options": {},
        "filtersUI": {
          "values": [
            {
              "lookupColumn": "Month",
              "lookupValue": "={{ $now.setZone('Asia/Kolkata').minus({ months: 1 }).toFormat('yyyy-LL') }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "d26b7f6c-68dd-4848-b666-ccc7794cf2a3",
      "name": "Last month's payroll",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "executeOnce": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Payroll tab: Key (e.g. 2026-09-E01), Month (yyyy-mm), Name, Email, Basic, HRA, Allowances, Overtime, Deductions, PF, ESI, TDS, Net pay, Days worked, Sent\nconst num = v => Number(String(v ?? '').replace(/[^0-9.-]/g, '')) || 0;\nconst rows = $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(r => r.Name && r.Sent !== 'yes');\nconst issues = [];\nfor (const r of rows) {\n  const calc = num(r.Basic) + num(r.HRA) + num(r.Allowances) + num(r.Overtime) - num(r.Deductions) - num(r.PF) - num(r.ESI) - num(r.TDS);\n  if (Math.abs(calc - num(r['Net pay'])) > 1) issues.push(`${r.Name}: net pay ${r['Net pay']} but the parts add up to ${calc}`);\n  if (!r.Email) issues.push(`${r.Name}: no email`);\n}\nreturn [{ json: { month: $now.setZone('Asia/Kolkata').minus({ months: 1 }).toFormat('LLLL yyyy'), count: rows.length, total_net: rows.reduce((s, r) => s + num(r['Net pay']), 0), issues, rows } }];"
      },
      "id": "b31c1bd5-f4a2-4689-836c-c3833e11b29b",
      "name": "Totals + checks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You check a small Indian business's payroll before payslips go out. Month: {{ $json.month }}. Employees: {{ $json.count }}. Total net pay: ₹{{ $json.total_net }}.\nProblems found by code: {{ JSON.stringify($json.issues) }}\nRows: {{ JSON.stringify($json.rows) }}\n\nok = true only if the code found no problems and nothing else looks clearly wrong (a net pay far higher than others for the same role, negative values, 0 days worked with pay). summary: one line for the owner. issues: a short list of problems (empty if ok). Never change any number.",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "id": "8878279c-3eb4-4e21-9fad-dc9c33e669c7",
      "name": "AI payroll check",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [
        720,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.1
        }
      },
      "id": "445aae97-c402-48e9-bf22-ba8291fe9467",
      "name": "AI model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        660,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"summary\": \"8 payslips, total ₹1,86,400, all rows add up.\",\n  \"issues\": []\n}"
      },
      "id": "10594758-f6fc-4c3b-8fa9-3b054aad1d81",
      "name": "JSON shape",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        860,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.ok }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "505c68e6-0fbf-4014-acb1-9be88181894d",
      "name": "All OK?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const t = $('Totals + checks').first().json;\nconst rs = v => '₹' + Number(v || 0).toLocaleString('en-IN');\nconst line = (k, v) => `<tr><td style=\"padding:4px 12px\">${k}</td><td style=\"padding:4px 12px;text-align:right\">${rs(v)}</td></tr>`;\nreturn t.rows.map(r => ({ json: { Key: r.Key, Name: r.Name, Email: r.Email, subject: `Payslip – ${t.month}`,\n  html: `<p>Hello ${r.Name},</p><p>Your payslip for <b>${t.month}</b> (${r['Days worked'] || '-'} days worked):</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;font-family:Arial\">` +\n    line('Basic', r.Basic) + line('HRA', r.HRA) + line('Allowances', r.Allowances) + line('Overtime', r.Overtime) + line('Deductions', -Number(r.Deductions || 0)) +\n    line('PF', -Number(r.PF || 0)) + line('ESI', -Number(r.ESI || 0)) + line('TDS', -Number(r.TDS || 0)) +\n    `<tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px\"><b>Net pay</b></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:right\"><b>${rs(r['Net pay'])}</b></td></tr></table>` +\n    `<p>Questions? Reply to this email.</p><p>– YOUR BUSINESS NAME</p>` } }));"
      },
